<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle trade inactive - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle trade inactive - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed. Inquiry moderate, demand light. Feedlots are current.</p>
<p>Sales confirmed for the week to date on 86,000 head including 30,200 head or about 35 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle. Asking prices 63.00-64.00, bids 62.00-62.50. Last sales at 63.00 on Wednesday. Confirmed - none</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
